sign errors, traceability problems, and, ultimately, higher costs. A model-based development process has many benefits and should be considered if growing complexity is breaking down your current development process. Benefits of Model-Based Engineering Eliminate documents. The model is connected to the design process eliminating the need for document generation. Design envelope. The model provides engineering with an implementation “design envelope,” providing freedom and guidance to the development team. Eliminate errors. Verification events defined in the model assure the consistency between the design and implementation. Traceability. The model history provides traceability eliminating the “how did we get here” experience. Transition to Detailed Design Today’s biggest challenge for model-based design is transitioning to implementation or detailed design. Many companies convert their model back to documents, disconnecting the model from the design process. Ideally, a design envelope for each E/E subsystem is directly transferred and exposed to the design teams for implementation. Implementation Assignments The model is segmented into work assignments for implementation. Imagine an aircraft with hundreds of E/E subsystems and design teams. The model-to-design team connection remains intact throughout the design process keeping the model relevant. Each design team has access to only their work assignment. Exposing the Model to Detailed Design Today’s biggest challenge for model-based design is transitioning to implementation or detailed design. Many companies convert their model back to documents, disconnecting the model from the design process. The design envelope for each E/E subsystem is directly transferred and exposed to the design teams for implementation. CR-8000 for PCB Subsystems CR-8000 is an advanced 3D PCB subsystem development platform. It’s the ability to build and optimize complete PCB subsystems that include multiple boards, mechanical enclosure, power, and SI analysis. Utilizing the model architecture and requirements, CR-8000 can verify the proposed design meets model requirements before and during detailed design. E3.series for Electrical Subsystems E3.series is an industry-leading wire harness and control panel design platform. Complex wire harness designs can be designed, visualized, and connected to manufacturing. Extensive design rule checks eliminate common errors. Integration with leading MCAD tools provides 3D analysis. CR-8000 PCB connector information can be directly imported. E3.series Genesys Connector Verification Events A critical part of E/E subsystem implementation is verifying requirements throughout the design process. GENESYS offers verification events that ensure model and implementation consistency. Verification gates would include architecture, design, and release to manufacturing. Verification alignment at the subsystem level adds convenience and efficiency. Learn More Features and Benefits Digital Engineering Model-Based Engineering supports Digital Engineering methods. MBE utilizes a model-based approach as opposed to a document-based. The product model is used to drive wire harness and PCB detailed design. Learn more Product Model The product model is constructed in GENESYS using system engineering methods. The product model or system context includes the product ecosystem. An example of the product ecosystem is the operating environment. Learn more Connected Model Model-Based Engineering supports a connected model design process. A model created in GENESYS is used to pass a design envelope to the development team for wire harness design and PCB design. Model Access Model-Based Engineering provides product model access to diagrams, requirements, and parameters for viewing by the design team. The design team can access a particular component or subsystem. Model Transfer Using the GENESYS Connector the component or subsystem architecture is directly transferred to E3.series for wire harness design. The design envelope is accessible providing diagrams, requirements, and parameters. 3D Detailed Design Using E3.series for wire harness design and CR-8000 for PCB provides 3D capabilities that are necessary for today’s complex designs. Learn more about E3.series Learn more about CR-8000 Product Model Verification GENESYS provides the ability to create verification events composed of verification requirements. Each verification event provides a design process checkpoint to assure model consistency with implementation. An example of a verification gate would be a design review prior to manufacturing. Smart Manufacturing Smart manufacturing and digital engineering are equal partners in digital transformation. Smart manufacturing depends on data that is gathered by IIOT and analyzed using big data. Providing the manufacturing floor with design data ready for machine consumption is an important output of MBE. Digital Engineering eBook This eBook describes an MBSE based process for Electrical and Electronic design. The eBook begins with model content and structure with the purpose of implementation and the need for a “design envelope”. The biggest challenge in MBSE gaining broad adoption is making the model relevant through the product life cycle. Learn how you can overcome this daunting hurdle while maintaining the model as the single source of truth. Download Now Related Products Products April 01, 2020 Digital Thread The Digital Thread is a foundational element of a successful Digital Engineering implementation. Digital conversations involving procurement, design, manufacturing and field service replace email and paper documents. Decisions and rationale are captured and provide traceability. Read now Products March 08, 2020 Architecture-Driven Engineering Digital Engineering requires a model-based design process that begins in Systems Engineering. Zuken acquired Vitech Corporation, a leader in Systems Engineering practices and MBSE solutions, with the intent of implementing an E/E model-based design process. Read now Resources Pages October 15, 2024 ZIW + Integrate24 2024 Highlights Americas , ziw , Americas , Events , integrate24 , ZIW , ZIW 2024 , Zuken Blog February 12, 2024 Shaping Tomorrow: The Unstoppable Demand of Digital Engineering Digital Engineering , Electrical & Wire Harness , GENESYS , IoT , MBSE , PCB Design , System-level Design , Digital Engineering , GENESYS , Internet of Things (IoT) , MBSE , Blog Pages November 06, 2023 Digital Engineering Basics Webinar Series Electrical & Wire Harness , Digital Engineering , MBSE , Webinar Series Webinar October 11, 2023 A Systems Architecture and Modeling Challenge - Recap of the First Annual World Championships, Part II Webinar , Vitech , Zuken USA , Digital Engineering Got a Question? - Contact Zuken today For more information on how Zuken can help your design process, contact Zuken today. Contact us today Stay updated Be the first to know about product releases, webinars, white papers, tech tips and more when you sign up for our emails. Products, Solutions & Services Digital Engineering CR-8000 E3.series Data Management Resources Webinars Blog E3.series Test Drives White Papers Case Studies Software Viewer Customers Community Support Website (ZGS) Support Details New Products / Releases Training Courses Design Service Providers Email Preferences Why Zuken Our Company Our Process Our Technology Partners Press Releases Events Automotive Consumer Machinery Careers Contact Privacy Policy Terms and Conditions Cookies Accessibility Sitemap XML © 2026 Zuken Design Verification - Learn More - Zuken US Skip to content Blog Events Webinars Community Support Login Americas Links to a regional Zuken site English Deutsch French Italian Americas Polish Japanese Chinese (Simplified) Korean Chinese (Traditional) Products Digital Engineering Digital Engineering Next Generation Design System Model Development Model Systems or Processes Model-Based Product Development Model-B